verses.tf_bn:
① **«اِنْ هِیَ اِلَّاۤ اَسْمَاۤءٌ سَمَّیْتُمُوْهَاۤ اَنْتُمْ وَاٰبَاۤؤُكُمْ مَّاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ بِهَا مِنْ سُلْطٰنٍ»** — ‘এগুলো কিছু অন্তঃসারশূন্য মনগড়া নাম ব্যতীত আর কিছুই নয়, যা তোমরা এবং তোমাদের অজ্ঞ পিতৃপুরুষেরা রেখে নিয়েছ; যার পক্ষে আল্লাহ কোনো সনদ বা প্রমাণ অবতীর্ণ করেননি’;
② **«اِنْ یَّتَّبِعُوْنَ اِلَّا الظَّنَّ وَمَا تَهْوَی الْاَنْفُسُ»** — ‘তারা তো কেবল ভিত্তিহীন অলীক ধারণা এবং নিজেদের কুপ্রবৃত্তিরই অন্ধ অনুসরণ করে চলেছে’;
③ **«وَلَقَدْ جَاۤءَهُمْ مِّنْ رَّبِّهِمُ الْهُدٰی»** — ‘অথচ তাদের প্রতিপালকের পক্ষ থেকে সত্যের সুস্পষ্ট হিদায়াত ও পথনির্দেশ (কুরআন ও রাসূলের মাধ্যমে) তাদের কাছে উপস্থিত হয়েছে!’; যার ফলে তাদের কোনো ওজর অবশিষ্ট নেই।

verses.tf_en:
① **«اِنْ هِیَ اِلَّاۤ اَسْمَاۤءٌ سَمَّیْتُمُوْهَاۤ اَنْتُمْ وَاٰبَاۤؤُكُمْ مَّاۤ اَنْزَلَ اللّٰهُ بِهَا مِنْ سُلْطٰنٍ»** (They are nothing but some names that you have coined, you and your forefathers – Allah has not sent any proof for them;) — These alleged deities are nothing but empty, invented names which you and your misguided ancestors concocted out of thin air, for which Allah has revealed no authority, scripture, or proof whatsoever;
② **«اِنْ یَّتَّبِعُوْنَ اِلَّا الظَّنَّ وَمَا تَهْوَی الْاَنْفُسُ»** (They follow only guesses and their own desires;) — The polytheists follow nothing in their religious practices except wild conjectures, baseless superstitions, and the vile cravings of their lower souls (*hawa*);
③ **«وَلَقَدْ جَاۤءَهُمْ مِّنْ رَّبِّهِمُ الْهُدٰی»** (Whereas the guidance from their Lord has come to them.) — Even though unambiguous, luminous guidance, accompanied by miracles and an unblemished Prophet, has already arrived at their doorstep from their Cherishing Lord!

verses.tf_bn:
① **«وَلِلّٰهِ مَا فِی السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِی الْاَرْضِ»** — ‘এবং আকাশমণ্ডলী ও জমিনে যা কিছু বিদ্যমান, সবই একমাত্র আল্লাহরই মালিকানাধীন ও সার্বভৌম কর্তৃত্বাধীন’;
② **«لِیَجْزِیَ الَّذِیْنَ اَسَاۤءُوْا بِمَا عَمِلُوْا»** — ‘যাতে তিনি পাপাচারী দুষ্কৃতকারীদেরকে তাদের পাপকর্মের উপযুক্ত শাস্তি প্রদান করেন’;
③ **«وَیَجْزِیَ الَّذِیْنَ اَحْسَنُوْا بِالْحُسْنٰی»** — ‘এবং যারা নেক আমল ও সৎকর্ম করেছে, তাঁদেরকে পরম কল্যাণময় অনন্ত জান্নাত দ্বারা সর্বোত্তম প্রতিদান দান করেন!’

verses.tf_en:
① **«وَلِلّٰهِ مَا فِی السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِی الْاَرْضِ»** (And to Allah only belongs all whatever is in the heavens and all whatever is in the earth,) — And to Allah alone belongs all that is in the celestial heavens and all that is on the earth, in total sovereignty, ownership, and creation;
② **«لِیَجْزِیَ الَّذِیْنَ اَسَاۤءُوْا بِمَا عَمِلُوْا»** (In order to repay those who do evil for what they have done,) — So that He may requite the wicked and corrupt transgressors with just retribution for the evil deeds they committed;
③ **«وَیَجْزِیَ الَّذِیْنَ اَحْسَنُوْا بِالْحُسْنٰی»** (And give an excellent reward to those who do good.) — And that He may lavishly reward the righteous who excelled in faith and virtue with the most magnificent recompense—the eternal bliss and beauty of Paradise (*al-Husna*).

① **«اَلَّذِیْنَ یَجْتَنِبُوْنَ كَبٰۤئِرَ الْاِثْمِ وَالْفَوَاحِشَ اِلَّا اللَّمَمَ»** (Those who avoid the cardinal sins and lewdness, except that they approached it and refrained;) — Those virtuous believers who vigilantly shun the major, cardinal sins (*Kaba'ir al-Ithm*) and flagrant obscenities (*Fawahish*), excepting only minor, inadvertent lapses or passing thoughts (*al-Lamam*) from which they promptly desist with sincere remorse and repentance;
② **«اِنَّ رَبَّكَ وَاسِعُ الْمَغْفِرَةِ»** (Indeed your Lord’s mercy is limitless;) — For verily, the forgiveness and pardon of your Cherishing Lord is vast and all-encompassing, ready to erase the minor missteps of those who strive against major transgressions;
③ **«هُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِكُمْ اِذْ اَنْشَاَكُمْ مِّنَ الْاَرْضِ وَاِذْ اَنْتُمْ اَجِنَّةٌ فِیْ بُطُوْنِ اُمَّهٰتِكُمْ»** (He knows you very well – since He has created you from clay, and when you were foetuses in your mothers’ wombs;) — He is intimately aware of your innate weaknesses, predispositions, and secret states, since He originally created your father Adam from the dust of the earth and nurtured you when you were hidden embryos within the wombs of your mothers;
④ **«فَلَا تُزَكُّوْۤا اَنْفُسَكُمْ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَنِ اتَّقٰی»** (Therefore do not, on your own, claim yourselves to be clean; He well knows who are the pious.) — Therefore, do not boastfully proclaim your own absolute purity, piety, and virtue out of self-righteous conceit; for He alone knows best who truly possesses genuine, humble Taqwa (reverence of Allah) in the depths of their soul! [With this verse, Ruku 2 of Surah An-Najm is completed].
